# CP16.1 — serve the charts.
#
# The viewer rendered its charts at file:// and not at http://127.0.0.1:8002/.
# `viewer/index.html` asks for `../out/charts/<name>.png`; from the filesystem
# that resolves against the repo tree, and served from `/` it resolves to
# `/out/charts/<name>.png`, which had no route. The page was correct in one
# origin and silently broken in the other.
#
# The broken origin is the one that matters most for a live demo: screen 3 needs
# the API, so a judge who started the server to try the voice lab was the judge
# looking at a results screen with four empty boxes on it.

settle/api/app.py
viewer/index.html
tests/test_viewer.py
checkpoints/cp16_1.allowlist

# --- Mounted, not routed ------------------------------------------------------
#
# `app.mount("/out/charts", StaticFiles(...))`. A mount is a sub-application and
# does not enter the OpenAPI schema, so SPEC §16's "exactly three routes" is
# untouched and `test_WBH_1_the_app_declares_exactly_the_three_spec_routes`
# passes unchanged — which matters, because `tests/test_webhook.py` is not on
# this allowlist.
#
# CP14 tried the other shape: an `@app.get("/out/{asset:path}")` handler. That
# is a fourth route, it broke the §16 assertion, and it was dropped. The mount is
# what CP14 should have used and did not.
#
# `viewer/index.html` is unchanged. It was on the allowlist in case the paths had
# to move, and they did not — the whole point of fixing this at the server is
# that `../out/charts/<name>.png` keeps working from `file://`, which is where a
# judge with a cloned repo and nothing running actually is.

# --- VIW-6 ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Five tests, and the chart list is parsed out of the page rather than written
# down, so a chart added to the viewer without a route fails here instead of
# appearing broken to whoever opens it next.
#
#   file://    every src resolves to a real file under the repo
#   http://    every src returns 200, content-type image/png, PNG magic bytes
#   both       byte-identical between the two origins
#   surface    the mount did not widen the OpenAPI route table
#   scope      traversal and every other out/ path still 404
#
# Verified adversarially: with the mount removed, two of the five fail. VIW-4
# still passes — screens 1 and 2 render from file:// with no server, executed
# under Node with `fetch` throwing.
